«
@@ WeakAcid — a laboratory exercise: the pH of a weak acid, acetic acid
@@ (pKa = 4.756 at 25 °C), by the equation WeakAcid of the Labs section of
@@ config/equations.csv: a dilution C = C0·V1/V2 and the charge balance
@@ [H⁺] = [A⁻] + [OH⁻], that is
@@   10^(−pH) = C·Ka/(Ka + 10^(−pH)) + Kw/10^(−pH),  Ka = 10^(−pKa), Kw = 10^(−pKw)
@@ an equation in pH that ROOT solves. For C = 10⁻¹ … 10⁻⁸ mol/L, returns one
@@ line per concentration, tagged C=1E-k: { the pH found by ROOT, the school
@@ approximation pH ≈ ½(pKa − log C) }, which forgets the water and the part
@@ of the acid that dissociates.
@@ Author & design          : Jean Wilson
@@ Co-authors & programming  : Claude & Claude Code (Anthropic)
  4.756 'pKa' Sto 14 'pKw' Sto 100_mL 'V1' Sto 100_mL 'V2' Sto
  1 8 For wak
    10 wak Neg ^ →Num 'C0' Sto
    @ ROOT solves an unknown that already exists only from its value
    IfErr { C pH } Purge Then End
    'ROOT(ⒺWeakAcid;[C;pH];[0.01;4])' Eval Drop
    pH 3 RND 4.756 wak + 2 / 3 RND
    2 →List "C=1E-" wak →Text + →Tag
  Next
»
